BND-10: apply the rule-step clamp to the fixed step taken between events

Between [EVENTS], routing_getRoutingStep() returned the fixed routing step
before reaching the clamp that ends each step on the next control-rule time.
When RULE_STEP is not a multiple of ROUTING_STEP the clock then misses the
rule grid, NewRuleTime is never advanced, rules stop being evaluated, and
the clamp, once applied again near the next event, yields a negative step
(ERROR 107). Set routingStep to the fixed step instead of returning, so the
clamp that follows applies to it.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply BND-10_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/routing.c b/src/legacy/engine/routing.c
index 9a47f4b..edb9e5e 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/routing.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/routing.c
@@ -182,7 +182,7 @@ double routing_getRoutingStep(int routingModel, double fixedStep)
         else
         {
             date1 = getDateTime(NewRoutingTime + 1000.0 * fixedStep);
-            if ( date1 < Event[NextEvent].start ) return fixedStep;
+            if ( date1 < Event[NextEvent].start ) routingStep = fixedStep;
         }
     }
 
